From: Geliang Tang <tanggeliang@kylinos.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: add msk_is_mptcp() helper

Introduce msk_is_mptcp() to check whether a socket is an MPTCP socket
(IPPROTO_MPTCP on SOCK_STREAM), modeled after sk_is_tcp(). Unlike
sk_is_mptcp() which tests a TCP subflow socket, this helper takes an
MPTCP socket directly.

The naming follows the convention of rsk_is_mptcp() to distinguish it
from sk_is_mptcp(). This helper will be used alongside sk_is_tcp() to
add MPTCP support for BPF sockmap, Landlock and in other places where
MPTCP socket type checking is going to be needed.

Signed-off-by: Geliang Tang <tanggeliang@kylinos.cn>
Reviewed-by: Günther Noack <gnoack3000@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
